{
  "schema": 1,
  "kind": "native_visual_timing",
  "native_live_video": true,
  "lesson": "04_platform_installers",
  "fps": 30,
  "total_duration": 333.9333333333334,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "scene": 1,
      "speech_start": 0.0,
      "speech_end": 19.733333333333334,
      "scene_end": 19.733333333333334,
      "duration": 19.733333333333334,
      "text": "Open the official spaCR release on GitHub and, under Assets, download the installer for your operating system. These online installers download the Python runtime and scientific packages during setup.",
      "visual": "08_official_release",
      "longest_narration_duration": 19.715,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 2,
      "speech_start": 19.733333333333334,
      "speech_end": 39.0,
      "scene_end": 39.0,
      "duration": 19.266666666666666,
      "text": "On Windows, run the setup executable and follow its prompts. Leave automatic acceleration selected to use the supported hardware detected on your computer, or choose CPU-only operation if that is what you need.",
      "visual": "09_windows_guidance",
      "longest_narration_duration": 19.265000000000004,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 3,
      "speech_start": 39.0,
      "speech_end": 63.96666666666667,
      "scene_end": 63.96666666666667,
      "duration": 24.966666666666665,
      "text": "On macOS, open the universal package and follow the installer. Start spaCR from its application launcher, and allow the first-run downloads to finish. Read any security prompt and confirm that the package came from the official release.",
      "visual": "10_macos_guidance",
      "longest_narration_duration": 24.940000000000005,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 4,
      "speech_start": 63.96666666666667,
      "speech_end": 92.0,
      "scene_end": 92.0,
      "duration": 28.033333333333335,
      "text": "On Linux, make the downloaded installer executable, then run it from a terminal. Automatic acceleration selects a supported backend. The help lists dash dash torch-backend cpu for CPU-only operation, and dash dash skip-system-deps for computers that already have the Qt graphics libraries.",
      "visual": "11_linux_commands",
      "longest_narration_duration": 28.009999999999998,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 5,
      "speech_start": 92.0,
      "speech_end": 107.8,
      "scene_end": 107.8,
      "duration": 15.8,
      "text": "After setup, the installation profile records the selected backend. Check this when you want to confirm whether the runtime uses CPU or a supported accelerator.",
      "visual": "02_installer_backend",
      "longest_narration_duration": 15.799999999999997,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 6,
      "speech_start": 107.8,
      "speech_end": 120.2,
      "scene_end": 120.2,
      "duration": 12.4,
      "text": "Check the installed spaCR version. Keep it with your analysis notes, especially when you update the application later.",
      "visual": "03_installed_versions",
      "longest_narration_duration": 12.39,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 7,
      "speech_start": 120.2,
      "speech_end": 143.1,
      "scene_end": 143.1,
      "duration": 22.9,
      "text": "Setup asks about optional diagnostic sharing and account setup. Answer y only for the options you want; n, the default, keeps each one off. The Windows installer shows the same choices as checkboxes.",
      "visual": "07_privacy_keep_off",
      "longest_narration_duration": 22.88500000000002,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 8,
      "speech_start": 143.1,
      "speech_end": 170.36666666666667,
      "scene_end": 170.36666666666667,
      "duration": 27.266666666666666,
      "text": "In the current nightly interface, open Preferences and choose Performance. Select a profile for your computer. Laptop uses fewer resources; higher profiles allow more caching and background work. Start with a modest profile if memory is limited.",
      "visual": "14_current_nightly_performance",
      "longest_narration_duration": 27.24000000000001,
      "native_live_video": true
    },
    {
      "scene": 9,
      "speech_start": 170.36666666666667,
      "speech_end": 198.73333333333335,
      "scene_end": 198.73333333333335,
      "duration": 28.366666666666667,
      "text": "This recording installs spaCR version one point five point one point three. Released builds can show an older Home layout. Here is Home in the current nightly build, with Core, Data, Tools and Organism. Continue to Home screen and navigation for the current modules.",
      "visual": "13_current_nightly_home",
      "longest_narration_duration": 27.995000000000005,
      "native_live_video": true
    },
    {
      "scene": 10,
      "speech_start": 198.73333333333335,
      "speech_end": 228.03333333333336,
      "scene_end": 228.03333333333336,
      "duration": 29.3,
      "text": "Run spacr-doctor from the installed runtime if startup or a file format needs attention. In this recorded CPU installation, the backend check passes and the GPU probe is skipped. The warning says the optional CZI reader is missing; install that extra only if you need CZI files.",
      "visual": "05_doctor",
      "longest_narration_duration": 29.275000000000006,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 11,
      "speech_start": 228.03333333333336,
      "speech_end": 252.90000000000003,
      "scene_end": 252.90000000000003,
      "duration": 24.866666666666667,
      "text": "For installation problems, find install dot log and install-profile dot json in the installation directory. Review the logs before sharing them with a support request. Include your operating system and spaCR version so the problem is easier to diagnose.",
      "visual": "12_logs_and_versions",
      "longest_narration_duration": 24.849999999999994,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 12,
      "speech_start": 252.90000000000003,
      "speech_end": 276.03333333333336,
      "scene_end": 276.03333333333336,
      "duration": 23.133333333333333,
      "text": "On Windows, close spaCR, open Settings, then Apps and Installed apps. Choose spaCR and Uninstall. The installed Uninstall executable is another route to the same removal process. Keep your project folders separately.",
      "visual": "15_uninstall_windows",
      "longest_narration_duration": 23.10499999999999,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 13,
      "speech_start": 276.03333333333336,
      "speech_end": 307.1333333333334,
      "scene_end": 307.1333333333334,
      "duration": 31.1,
      "text": "On macOS, close spaCR and run the bundled uninstall-spacr script in Library slash Application Support slash spaCR. It removes the application and its system launchers. The per-user runtime in your own Library slash Application Support slash spaCR is separate; remove it only if you also want to discard that runtime.",
      "visual": "16_uninstall_macos",
      "longest_narration_duration": 31.089999999999975,
      "native_live_video": false
    },
    {
      "scene": 14,
      "speech_start": 307.1333333333334,
      "speech_end": 333.9333333333334,
      "scene_end": 333.9333333333334,
      "duration": 26.8,
      "text": "On Linux, close spaCR and run the uninstall-spacr script under your home folder, dot local slash share slash spacr. It removes the managed runtime and application launchers. Uninstallation does not require deleting your microscopy projects or their analysis results.",
      "visual": "17_uninstall_linux",
      "longest_narration_duration": 26.774999999999977,
      "native_live_video": false
    }
  ],
